{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLibObject\/4GLib14PointerWrapperP","doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/GWeakCapturing","doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/ObjectProtocol","doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeModuleProtocol","doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypePluginProtocol"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TypeModuleRef","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The model of ","type":"text"},{"code":"GTypeModule","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a dynamically loaded module which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"implements some number of types and interface implementations.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the module is loaded, it registers its types and interfaces"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"using [method"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GObject.TypeModule.register_type"},{"text":"] and","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[method","type":"text"},{"code":"GObject.TypeModule.add_interface","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"].","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"As long as any instances of these types and interface implementations","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"are in use, the module is kept loaded. When the types and interfaces","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"are gone, the module may be unloaded. If the types and interfaces"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"become used again, the module will be reloaded. Note that the last","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reference cannot be released from within the module code, since that"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would lead to the caller’s code being unloaded before ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_object_unref()"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"returns to it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keeping track of whether the module should be loaded or not is done by","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"using a use count - it starts at zero, and whenever it is greater than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"zero, the module is loaded. The use count is maintained internally by"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the type system, but also can be explicitly controlled by"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"[method"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GObject.TypeModule.use"},{"type":"text","text":"] and [method"},{"code":"GObject.TypeModule.unuse","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Typically, when loading a module for the first type, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_type_module_use()"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"will be used to load it so that it can initialize its types. At some later"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point, when the module no longer needs to be loaded except for the type"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"implementations it contains, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_type_module_unuse()"},{"text":" is called.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GTypeModule"},{"text":" does not actually provide any implementation of module","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"loading and unloading. To create a particular module type you must","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"derive from "},{"code":"GTypeModule","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and implement the load and unload functions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"code":"GTypeModuleClass","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeModuleRef","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" type acts as a lightweight Swift reference to an underlying "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GTypeModule"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"It exposes methods that can operate on this data type through "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeModuleProtocol"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeModuleRef","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" only as an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unowned"},{"type":"text","text":" reference to an existing "},{"code":"GTypeModule","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeModule","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (instead of "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeModuleRef","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") if you want to use Automatic Reference Counting for memory management of the underlying "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GTypeModule"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note","style":"note"}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TypeModuleRef"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"